{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Interaction Overview Diagram"}, {"type": "position", "content": 10}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about interaction overview diagrams."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Give detailed information related to UML and common related topics."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.  Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob10re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "characteristic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feature that describes something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You will have to be more specific about the characteristics of IODs."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob10aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "frame"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a static image among a series or a square where you can put something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As you can see here on my diagram, the nodes are frames."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob10aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "seem "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to appear, to look like or to resemble"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That seems complex."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob10aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "complex "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "composed of a lot of details "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  That seems complex."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob10aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "widely"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "extensively, comprehensively or largely"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can visualize widely the interactive behavior of a system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob10aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about other types of UML"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write the information about types of UML in your notebook."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your findings with your teacher and classmates"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I investigate about other types of UML"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about other types of UML"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about other types of UML"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Future with Will and Might"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">will</span> and <span class=\"strong\">might</span> to talk about predictions and possibilities in the future. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">will</span> to talk about voluntary actions, promises, and future predictions. To create statements, you just need to follow this grammatical structure: <br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <span class=\"strong\">Will</span> + Verb + Complement</div><br/><br/>  Examples: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Don't you know what an overview diagram is? Don't worry, I <span class=\"strong\">will</span> explain that to you. <br/> She <span class=\"strong\">will</span> include all the necessary information on the diagram. </span> <br/><br/>   You can also use <span class=\"strong\">might</span> to express possibility. To create statements, you just need to follow this grammatical structure: <br/><br/>  <div class=\"center_text\">Subject + <span class=\"strong\">Might</span> + Verb + Complement</div><br/><br/>  Examples: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">might</span> need to use a different diagram, the one we use is very confusing. <br/> He <span class=\"strong\">might</span> want to see the diagram we designed. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will explain to you an interaction overview diagram works. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You will have to be more specific about the characteristics of IODs."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I might have to do an IOD diagram at some point."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Prepositions of Place"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">prepositions of place</span> to help you locate objects in a space."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are many <span class=\"strong\">prepositions of place</span>; these are some of the most common: <br/><br/>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Regarding the features of interaction overview diagrams, we find the objects that take part in the interaction, the message flow that goes among those objects, a sequence where message flow, and an object organization. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "As you can see here on my diagram, the nodes are frames."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Preposition</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Use</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"In\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When an object is inside something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The information for the diagram is <span class=\\\"strong\\\">in</span> my drawer. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"On\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When an object is touching a surface. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I just drew the diagram we're using <span class=\\\"strong\\\">on</span> the blackboard. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"At\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you want to talk a specific place or section\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We need to succeed <span class=\\\"strong\\\">at</span> the implementation of the diagram. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"In front of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When something is before another object\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The company's servers are right <span class=\\\"strong\\\">in front of</span> your office. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Behind\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When something is in the back of something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">There are many important components <span class=\\\"strong\\\">behind</span> those schemes. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Hey, Janice! What are you doing? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janice</span>: Hello, John, I'm working on an interaction overview diagram to show how online shopping works. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: That seems complex. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janice</span>: It is not! I will explain to you an interaction overview diagram works. The first thing you need to know is that an interaction overview diagram or IOD is a variant of a UML activity diagram, but instead of drawing activities, we draw interactions. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Ok, and what can I do with an IOD diagram? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janice</span>: Well, You can visualize widely the interactive behavior of a system. On an IOD diagram, we can see how several interactions work together to show a system's functionality."}, {"time": "54000", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Cool! I might have to do an IOD diagram at some point, what do I have to take into account to create one? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janice</span>: There are some important details that you need to consider.  As you can see here on my diagram, the nodes are frames; and there are two types of frames. The first one is an interaction frame which represents sequence, communication, timing, and overview diagrams. The second one is an occurrence frame that shows activities and operations. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: I see. You will have to be more specific about the characteristics of IODs. Do those diagrams have key features for me to be able to identify them?"}, {"time": "101000", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Janice</span>: Definitely, regarding the features of interaction overview diagrams, we find the objects that take part in the interaction, the message flow that goes among those objects, a sequence where message flow, and an object organization.     <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: I understand. And I assume that those shapes are decision diamonds, right? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Janice</span>: Exactly. If you want to create your own diagram, you will need to take into account all the things I mentioned. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Thanks, Janice."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n4le02ob10re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n4le02ob10re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": "01.jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "02.jpg", "type": "img"}], "type": "static", "_data": [], "id": 2, "title": ""}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": "01t.jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "02t.jpg", "type": "img"}, {"value": "03t.jpg", "type": "img"}], "type": "static", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain how the interaction overview diagram works. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give details about the interaction overview diagram."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can identify key features related to interaction overview diagram."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are the most common types of diagrams in UML?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you think it is easy to organize items on a diagram? Why? Why not? "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{